# The examples inherit the superproject's configuration and switch off one
# check and one option.
#
# bugprone-exception-escape.CheckMain treats every example's main as a
# function that should not throw. An example is a short program that lets
# what the standard library may throw, a std::bad_alloc or a
# std::length_error from a container that grows, end the process uncaught,
# the way Boost's own examples do; that is main's ordinary role, not a
# defect. The check stays on for everything else: a noexcept function, a
# destructor, a move or a swap.
#
# bugprone-forward-declaration-namespace reports a tag declared and never
# referenced when another namespace declares one of the same name. Three
# examples include webcpp::crypto beside hash, and both libraries name their
# backend tags alike on purpose (backends::openssl, backends::bearssl, each
# declared and never defined), so every example of both reports the tag it
# does not name, in either library's header. The check stays on for the
# library's headers (the aggregate) and its tests.
---
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -bugprone-forward-declaration-namespace
CheckOptions:
  - key: bugprone-exception-escape.CheckMain
    value: 'false'
